Whisper: the add-ons Whisper ships are never checked for updates at addons.mozilla.org

What: an add-on update check (the daily background check, the check when an add-on
is installed, after an application update or when the user asks) for an add-on
named in the pref whisper.extensions.pinned ends at once as a check that found no
update, without a request.
Why: Whisper ships uBlock Origin (and later more add-ons) pinned to a version and a
SHA-256 (gecko/ubo.env) and updates them only with Whisper builds. Firefox's check
asked versioncheck-bg.addons.mozilla.org about each one every day and on the first
start, telling Mozilla which add-ons the profile has. Add-ons the user installs
still update as in Firefox.
---
--- a/toolkit/mozapps/extensions/internal/XPIInstall.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/mozapps/extensions/internal/XPIInstall.sys.mjs
@@ -3175,6 +3175,20 @@
     aReason == AddonManager.UPDATE_WHEN_NEW_APP_INSTALLED;
   this.isUserRequested = aReason == AddonManager.UPDATE_WHEN_USER_REQUESTED;
 
+  // Whisper: the add-ons Whisper ships (whisper.extensions.pinned) update with
+  // Whisper only, never from addons.mozilla.org: no update check asks for them
+  // (patches/0035-pinned-add-ons.patch). The check ends as one that found nothing.
+  if (
+    Services.prefs
+      .getStringPref("whisper.extensions.pinned", "")
+      .split(",")
+      .includes(aAddon.id)
+  ) {
+    this._parser = { cancel() {} };
+    Services.tm.dispatchToMainThread(() => this.onUpdateCheckComplete([]));
+    return;
+  }
+
   // If bug 2032469 changes the policy behavior, this will need to be updated.
   let updateURL =
     Services.policies?.getExtensionSettings(aAddon.id)?.update_url?.href ||
